"entity": {
"name": "EUROBANK S.A.",
"description": "Eurobank SA provides banking and commercial services. It operates through the following segments: Retail, Corporate, Global Markets & Asset Management, International, Investment Property, Remedial and Servicing Strategy (RSS) and Others. The Retail segment engages in customer current accounts, savings, deposits and investment savings products, credit and debit cards, consumer loans, small business banking, and mortgages. The Corporate segment engages in current accounts, deposits, overdrafts, loans and other credit facilities, foreign currency and derivative products for corporate entities, custody and clearing services, cash management and trade services, and investment banking services including corporate finance and merger and acquisition advice. The Global Markets & Asset Management segment engages in financial instruments trading, services to institutional investors, as well as specialized financial advice and intermediation. The International segment engages in operations in Bulgaria, Cyprus, Luxembourg, Romania, and Serbia. The Investment Property segment engages in investment property activities related to a diversified portfolio of commercial real estate assets. The RSS segment engages in the management of non-performing assets, property management of repossessed assets, and administration of notes from loan securitizations. The Other segment includes property management, investing activities, private banking for medium and high net worth individuals, Eurolife Insurance results, and outcomes from transformation projects and initiatives. The company was founded in 1990 and is headquartered in Athens, Greece.",
